    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0520" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.00/3–1045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Rumanian Prime Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Groza</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President
                        Roosevelt </hi><anchor n="19" xml:id="d369-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-10T16:00:00+02:00">March 10, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">The President</hi>: At the moment of the
                    installation of the Rumanian Government I send greetings to the President of the
                    United States imbued with the highest purposes in combat by which United Nations
                    are rendering Hitler Germany powerless. Rumanian Government gives assurance that
                    Rumania will make all efforts to defeat fascism quickly. Rumanian Government
                    hopes that in that way a new international situation will be created which will
                    allow of participation in the work of organizing peaceably the world of
                    tomorrow. Hurrah for the common combat of the peoples to render fascism
                    powerless, hurrah for Rumanian-American friendship.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dr. Petru Groza</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President of the Council</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d369-f1" n="19" type="source" xml:id="d369-f1-content">
                <p>This message was sent in Rumanian via commercial cable. The White House referred
                    it to the Department of State on March 12 for translation and appropriate
                    action. The Department recommended that no reply be made; see telegram 157,
                    March 27, 10 a.m., to Bucharest, <ref target="#pg524">p. 524</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
